WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.563
Row grain is one of the most

00:00:01.589 --> 00:00:05.777
important design habits in this course Grain

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:07.974
answers the question what does one row

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.347
represent For a patient table one row

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.165
may represent one patient For appointment one

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:19.731
row may represent one scheduled encounter For

00:00:19.758 --> 00:00:22.613
service one row may represent one reusable

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:26.587
service definition For appointment service one row

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.823
may represent one service used during one

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.079
appointment Problems begin when one row tries

00:00:33.105 --> 00:00:35.355
to represent several different subjects at the

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:39.457
same time Before choosing columns for any

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.128
table finish the sentence one row equals

00:00:42.154 --> 00:00:45.673
one what If that sentence is hard

00:00:45.686 --> 00:00:47.700
to complete the table design may be

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.371
mixing several concepts and should be reconsidered

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:51.621
before implementation
